        "func": "// (Assuming your MQTT node is set to output a parsed JSON Object)\nvar data = msg.payload;\n\n// 2. Check if the specific property exists\nif (data && data.hasOwnProperty(\"isSlotOccupied\")) {\n    \n    msg.payload = {};\n    const newObj = {};\n    for (const key in data.isSlotOccupied) {\n    // Implicitly converts string key to int for math\n        const newKey = parseInt(key) % 10; \n        newObj[newKey] = data.isSlotOccupied[key];\n    }\n    \n    msg.payload = newObj;\n    \n    return msg;\n}\n\n// 5. If the property doesn't exist, return null\n// This stops the flow completely, so the LED ignores this message.\nreturn null;",
